<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17463" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">făber</span></b> , bra, brum,
			adj.
		1. faber, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>workmanlike</i>, <i>skilful</i>, <i>ingenious</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 159</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. F. 3, 383</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">levitas speculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 282</span></i>
			. —<i>Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signaculum faberrimum anuli aurei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. p. 346</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fā^bre</span></b> , <i>in a
				workmanlike manner</i>, <i>skilfully</i>, <i>ingeniously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc factum est fabre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. 1, 2, 23</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Stich. 4, 1, 64</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">teres trabs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
				14</span></i>
			,  320; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Exod. 35, 33</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sigillatum vitrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 123</span></i>
			 (cf. fabrefacio).—<i>Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facta navis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 262 al.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aptare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 20, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
